{"body":"The original Chromium verification suite reported one unexpected failure when returning from a county detail page to `/counties?p=2`: the outgoing list scroll was approximately 900–911px, but the returned list settled at 100px and the existing `afterY > 100` contract failed.\n\nObserved in [run 38009357220, original Chromium job](https://github.com/Rodgers31/audit_app/actions/runs/38009357220/job/114085507802), frozen combined commit `b70996e9e1e28f7e6b445f0d3c41be3681fadd61`. The preserved Playwright trace records returned positions 86 → 100, still 100 after the test's 800ms observation. Original public cohort: 257 passed, 11 existing skips, one unexpected failure, zero retries/flaky cases. Other original cohorts passed. Test: `frontend/e2e/smart-back.spec.ts:72`, assertion at line 100.\n\nThe application/components/navigation/fixture/test/Playwright-config bytes are unchanged from the previously successful accepted commit `26969ae7c9d4c70e423569eac8b182cecd1d6d2d`. An exact-source isolated macOS production-config replay passed the original targeted case five times without retries; that does not reproduce Linux hosted geometry or establish the cause. Investigation remains open; timing, layout and history restoration need to be distinguished with instrumentation rather than guessed.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Establish a reproducible cause or a bounded instrumented explanation using the unchanged original case and production-config Chromium; preserve failure trace and runtime/viewport/layout identities.\n- If the app loses/clamps a legitimate stored scroll position, correct restoration without losing query/filter/history behavior and demonstrate an actual failing control followed by a pass.\n- If the test observes an unfinished transition, use an observable state contract, retaining meaningful saved-position assertions and the original suite inventory.\n- Verify original full Chromium suite with no unexpected or retried failures; retain original failure evidence and label every later run by its actual source/attempt.\n\nDo not classify this as a new regression in PRs #588/#590/#592/#593/#596 solely from the failed combined run. No navigation source was changed by that batch. No assertion widening, fixed-sleep increase or quarantine has been applied.\n\nDeduplication: complete all-state issue census (295 issues, six REST pages, including closed records) checked for smart-back/scroll-restoration/scroll-position findings; no matching ticket.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOPmNsm88AAAABayerew","author":{"login":"Rodgers31"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"The fresh full Linux original Chromium replay passes all 323 inventoried cases: 312 passes/11 existing fixmes, zero unexpected or flaky outcomes. The smart-back assertion and cohort inventory are unchanged; no retries, weakened assertion, extra sleep or quarantine was introduced. The prior actual hosted failure restored only Y=100 after leaving around Y=900. Bounded local timing/geometry/CPU controls did not reproduce its cause. A successful replay does not resolve that observation: this issue remains open for a deterministic root-cause investigation and repair.\n\nAll seven jobs passed in [full hosted run 38014890047](https://github.com/Rodgers31/audit_app/actions/runs/38014890047), attempt 1, on frozen combined commit `855ab42cd0815edbba6f94d6a376c60cb7dd7890`. Actual merged main `f6c31e271297eece52f34102dc40a1e2ed7069a8` has the identical tree `69ddfad6deb814dd08fdaee2db2d512d73e14c78`. This is tree equivalence; hosted evidence remains bound to its actual tested commit. Repository Actions and all five static workflows are verified OFF; no production migration, reconciliation, restart or activation occurred.\n","createdAt":"2026-10-10T02:27:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Rodgers31/audit_app/issues/601#issuecomment-6092729211","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":601,"state":"OPEN","title":"P2: investigate intermittent county smart-back scroll restoration in Chromium","url":"https://github.com/Rodgers31/audit_app/issues/601"}
